    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0448" n="372" xml:id="pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.404/157: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-05T10:00:00+01:00">November 5, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 5—6:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>215. State of highest confusion prevails in Evangelical Church affairs. Kerrl
                    under party pressure seems to be turning strongly against Confessional group.
                    Secret police forbade last Friday reopening of Confessional Seminary and
                    Propaganda Ministry interfering with church press to such an extent that even
                    new “neutral committees” have protested and it is not impossible they may
                    resign. Confessional authorities demanding retirement of Reichsbishop Müller and
                    two radical German Christian bishops and are understood to be discussing
                    advisability of calling a fourth national synod.</p>
                <p>Schacht<anchor n="25" xml:id="d286-f1"/> has now publicly intimated imminence of
                    restrictions on Jewish businesses but in accordance with previous standpoint has
                    forbidden interference pending promulgation of new regulations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d286-f1" n="25" xml:id="d286-f1-content">
                <p>Hjalmar Schacht, Minister of Economic Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
